    "description": "Sign_Up__c records must originate ONLY from the Study Link Click automation (BUILD-04 / SLC async flow). Reps creating them by hand produces records with no SLC lineage, no deal attribution, and no payout code — unfixable downstream.\n\nBuild:\n\n* Remove Create on Sign_Up__c from the Rep profile and Rep permission set group. Removing Create automatically hides the New button on list views, related lists, and the global Create menu — no separate button work needed.\n\n* Confirm the SLC automation still creates records: record-triggered/autolaunched Flow runs in system context, so it is unaffected. Test end-to-end as a Rep user, not as admin.\n\n* Audit for any rep-facing screen flow or quick action that creates a Sign-Up in user context — those would break and must be rerouted through an autolaunched subflow.\n\n* Confirm reps retain Read + Edit on Sign_Up__c (they still action records) and can still Clone-block cleanly — verify Clone is not exposed.\n\n* Check the same for any rep-accessible Sign-Up related list on Account/Deal.\n\nCaveat: with Create removed, reps also cannot create Sign-Ups during UAT test scripts — update the UAT scripts (BUILD-106) so testers use an admin/ops user or a seeded SLC to generate records.\n\nEffort: \\~1-2h incl. end-to-end test.\n\nSource: Kobi, 2026-08-05.",
